 "inference": [
  "The two fields are the disabled-state thresholds; which is which cannot be told from the CB90, where both are 400. Field_1a7c18f1 is the lower or equal value in most files but the larger one in 4 (VB_VEH_Airplane_MQ9, VB_VEH_Helicopter_MH47_SP, VB_VEH_SP_Assault_Airplane_JAS39, VB_VEH_Stationary_Turret_CROWS), so no fixed order can be read from the values.",
  "Tanks (1200 health) store 200 and 400; the JLTV and Marauder (800) 200 and 300; attack helicopters 200 and 300. If a vehicle turns critical at the lower number and recovers at the higher, a tank is critical below 200 and recovers above 400; that reading is an inference.",
  "Registry MaxHealth equals the root health field for the CB90, a second naming of Field_9040392c as vehicle health (L3334).",
  "The 80 percent regeneration slowdown itself was not found as a stored number (L3346)."
 ],
